2. Definitions

"Copyright Holder" means lewonn / LWNX DSP.

"Software" means PHOQER in source or compiled form, but excludes third-party
material except when a section expressly discusses that material.

"Modified Software" means any work based on or incorporating a substantial
part of the Project Material, including a modification, fork, port, or reuse of
PHOQER source code in another software product.

"User Content" means music, audio recordings, performances, compositions,
sound design, audiovisual works, games, broadcasts, streams, and user-created
presets produced through normal use of the Software. User Content does not
include the Software, Modified Software, source code, or original project
assets themselves.

"Commercial Software Activity" means selling, licensing, renting, charging
for access to, commercially distributing, or otherwise receiving direct or
indirect compensation for the Software or Modified Software. It also includes
paid development for an employer or client when that work creates or modifies
the Software or Modified Software, and donations or sponsorships offered in
direct connection with distributing or developing that software. It does not
include creating, using, publishing, performing, licensing, or monetizing User
Content.

"Noncommercial" means not primarily intended for or directed toward commercial
advantage or monetary compensation for the person exercising the licensed
rights. Using an ordinary commercial code-hosting or distribution service does
not by itself make an activity commercial when that person receives no direct
or indirect compensation from the activity.

